# Brief for chapter authors

You are writing one chapter of *{{TITLE}}*. Read, in this order:

1. `STYLE_GUIDE.md` (rules, chapter structure, figures, code, compile check, review rubric)
2. `docs/chapter-template.tex` (the mandatory skeleton)
3. `docs/requirements.md` (what the book must cover; your topic's priority, its place in
   the schedule, its coding exercise and milestone)
4. your specification `docs/specs/<id>.md` (every "must cover" item is mandatory)
5. `Overleaf/textbook.sty` (macros, boxes, TikZ styles; use them, do not redefine them)
6. `docs/style-test.tex` (a short chapter that exercises every environment; copy its idioms)

## Deliverables (paths relative to the repository root)

| File | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `Overleaf/chapters/chNN-slug.tex` | yes | overwrite the placeholder; 900–1500 lines |
| `Overleaf/figures/chNN/*.tex` | yes (≥4) | one `tikzpicture` per file, no `figure` env, no `\label` |
| `Overleaf/figures/data/chNN-*.dat` | if plotting data | generated by a script below |
| `Overleaf/code/chNN_slug.py` | yes | full implementation with passing self-test |
| `Overleaf/code/figures/gen_chNN_*.py` | if generated figures | fixed seed, writes the .dat/.tex |
| `Overleaf/appendices/solutions/chNN-solutions.tex` | yes | 2–4 `solution` environments for your exercises |
| `Overleaf/appendices/glossary/chNN-terms.tex` | yes | 6–15 lines `\item[Term] One-sentence definition.` |
| `Overleaf/bib/chNN-extra.bib` | if new references | only entries you are certain about |

Do **not** edit `main.tex`, `textbook.sty`, `references.bib`, other chapters, or the front
matter. If you need a macro or a package, describe it in your final report.

## Working method

* Write the chapter text first, in a few large writes, not many tiny edits; then the code,
  then the figures, then solutions and glossary terms.
* Write the code before the worked example's numbers: every number in the text comes from
  running it.
* Compile with `cd Overleaf && ./build.sh chNN-slug`; read `build/only-chNN-slug.log` for
  errors; `pdftotext build/only-chNN-slug.pdf - | head -400` to proofread.
* Macro/function names in `\SetKwFunction`, `\newcommand` and listing labels must be
  unique across the book: prefix them with your chapter topic. Prefer no new `\newcommand`.
* ASCII only inside listings and `.dat` files. `--` for en-dashes in text, `\%` for percent.
* Cross-references to other chapters use the labels in the book map below; never claim what
  another chapter contains beyond what the map says.
* Finish only when: build status 0, no errors, no undefined labels of your own, the
  self-test passes, and the chapter has every mandatory section of the template.

## Final report (your last message, at most 300 words)

Files written; page count of your chapter; number of figures/tables/algorithms/listings/
exercises; what the self-test checks; any reference you added; anything the editor must do.

